1. INSTALLATION AND VERIFICATION PIPELINE
============================================================

Prerequisites: a working R installation and the devtools package.

Step 1 — Install devtools if you do not already have it:

    install.packages("devtools")

Step 2 — Install StatARPLS directly from GitHub:

    devtools::install_github("tardagur/StatARPLS")

Step 3 — Load the package:

    library(StatARPLS)

Step 4 — Clone or download the repository locally so you can run the
automated test suite (devtools::test() must be run from inside the
package source directory, not from an installed copy):

    git clone https://github.com/tardagur/StatARPLS.git
    setwd("StatARPLS")

Step 5 — Run the automated test suite:

    devtools::test()

Expected result at this snapshot stage:

    [ FAIL 0 | WARN 0 | SKIP 0 | PASS 8 ]

If your result differs from this, please note the exact output you see
and include it in your feedback — a different pass count most likely
means your local R or package versions differ from the ones this
snapshot was built and tested against, and that mismatch is itself
useful information for me to record.

Step 6 (optional but recommended) — Run a full package check:

    devtools::check()

This performs a stricter validation than devtools::test() alone
(documentation consistency, namespace correctness, etc.) and is a good
second data point if anything in Step 5 looks unexpected.


